---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GradeScale from '../components/GradeScale';

const title = "Grading Bracket & Grade Scale Chart | Pass My Finals";
const description = "Convert percentages to letter grades using our standard grading bracket and college grade scale chart. See exactly how your grades translate.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<main class="relative">
		<header class="pt-20 pb-12 text-center px-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
			<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight text-black dark:text-white leading-tight">
				Grade <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 to-indigo-500">Scale</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">
				Master the conversion between percentages, letter grades, and grade points. Choose a preset or customize to match your school's grading bracket.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="pb-20">
			<GradeScale client:load />
		</section>

		<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/30 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-white/5 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 prose dark:prose-invert">
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-black dark:text-white mb-6">Understanding Your Grading Bracket</h2>
				<p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-300">
					A <strong>grading bracket</strong> (or grading scale) is the system schools use to determine the letter grade you receive based on your course percentage. While the standard 4.0 scale is widely used across the United States, your specific bracket can drastically change whether a 89% is a B+ or an A-.
				</p>
				
				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Standard High School vs College Grade Scales</h3>
				<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400">
					High schools typically use a flat 10-point grading bracket (A = 90-100%, B = 80-89%, etc.). Colleges and universities frequently use a +/- system (A- = 90-92%, A = 93-100%). This distinction is why we allow you to toggle between presets in our tool above.
				</p>
				
				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">How is a Grade Curve Applied?</h3>
				<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400">
					If a professor "curves" an exam, they are effectively lowering the minimum percentage required to enter the next grading bracket. For example, if the top score was an 85%, the professor might shift the entire A bracket down so that 85% equals an A.
				</p>

				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Ready to calculate your finals?</h3>
				<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400">
					Now that you understand your grading bracket, use our <a href="/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">Finals Calculator</a> to figure out exactly what score you need on your final exam to pass. If you're looking at the bigger picture, check out our <a href="/gpa-calculator" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">Cumulative GPA Calculator</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
